WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.492 --> 00:00:02.791
- [Carolyn] To go to a cocktail party

00:00:02.791 --> 00:00:04.409
and to see an hors d'oeuvres

00:00:04.409 --> 00:00:06.220
that has a toothpick sticking up from it,

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.885
the point of that toothpick

00:00:07.885 --> 00:00:10.396
makes me feel shocks of electricity

00:00:10.396 --> 00:00:12.354
down the back of my legs.

00:00:12.354 --> 00:00:14.771
People are perplexed by that.

00:00:18.512 --> 00:00:20.071
My name is Carolyn Hart,

00:00:20.071 --> 00:00:22.949
I have mirror-touch synesthesia.

00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:26.079
Mirror-touch synesthesia is
a conflation of the senses.

00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:27.714
Mirror-touch synesthesia is
a conflation of the senses.

00:00:27.714 --> 00:00:30.596
The things that you see
are felt on your skin.

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:33.331
The things that you see
are felt on your skin.

00:00:33.331 --> 00:00:35.750
If I see another person's injuries,

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.289
well I feel that in my own body.

00:00:38.289 --> 00:00:40.307
If I see someone get touched,

00:00:40.307 --> 00:00:42.224
I feel that on my skin.

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:45.292
I'm a massage therapist.

00:00:45.292 --> 00:00:47.748
I think my mirror-touch synesthesia

00:00:47.748 --> 00:00:49.172
has really helped me.

00:00:49.172 --> 00:00:50.490
When someone tells me

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.353
what they're feeling in their body,

00:00:52.353 --> 00:00:53.766
well I feel it in my body.

00:00:53.766 --> 00:00:57.933
And I think it makes me more
able to help that person.

00:00:59.214 --> 00:01:00.375
Every single day

00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:01.208
Every single day

00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:02.400
I will see something that
triggers waves of pain.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.204
I will see something that
triggers waves of pain.

00:01:07.204 --> 00:01:10.358
It makes it really hard
for me to participate

00:01:10.358 --> 00:01:12.817
in a lot of contemporary entertainment.

00:01:12.817 --> 00:01:14.683
Like I really love Game of Thrones

00:01:14.683 --> 00:01:16.501
Like I really love Game of Thrones

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:20.668
and I can't watch the program
because it's so violent.

00:01:23.575 --> 00:01:26.872
I also have really positive experiences.

00:01:26.872 --> 00:01:30.136
When I watch ballet I
feel my muscles fire.

00:01:30.136 --> 00:01:32.268
When I watch ballet I
feel my muscles fire.

00:01:32.268 --> 00:01:35.109
When I see them executing pirouettes

00:01:35.109 --> 00:01:36.042
When I see them executing pirouettes

00:01:36.042 --> 00:01:38.450
I feel like I'm spinning.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.283
And that's not an emotional sense of

00:01:39.283 --> 00:01:42.156
And that's not an emotional sense of

00:01:42.156 --> 00:01:45.489
"Gee, this is really lovely
and so beautiful to watch."

00:01:45.489 --> 00:01:47.050
I feel it in my body.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.327
I feel it in my body.

00:01:48.327 --> 00:01:50.192
I can't control it.

00:01:50.192 --> 00:01:52.429
If I was to lose my synesthesia,

00:01:52.429 --> 00:01:54.057
I would lose part of myself

00:01:54.057 --> 00:01:57.890
that would be irretrievable
and irreplaceable.

